# =============================================================================
# Native-dev process environment (NOT the compose/helm deployment).
#
#   cp docker/.env.app.example docker/.env.app   # then fill in real values
#
# `make up` / `make backend` / `make worker-knowledge` source this file before
# starting backend, Celery and the Linsight worker, so a value set here reaches
# the process that actually does the work — document parsing runs in the
# knowledge worker, not the API.
#
# Why a separate file instead of reusing docker/.env: that one is compose's
# deployment file and carries keys the backend itself reads (BISHENG_PRO,
# BISHENG_RUNTIME_CONTROL_SECRET, BISHENG_RUNTIME_PAYLOAD_KEY, …). Sourcing it
# into a native dev process would silently change platform behaviour. This file
# is only for per-developer secrets.
#
# docker/.env.app is git-ignored — nothing in here should ever be committed.
# =============================================================================

# PaddleOCR hosted jobs API (knowledges.paddle_ocr.api_key_env names this var).
# Required only when the OCR provider is paddle_ocr against a /jobs URL.
# Get a token from the AIStudio console; rotate it if it ever lands in git.
PADDLE_OCR_TOKEN=

# Example of the same pattern for the MinerU V4 provider (already supported).
# MINERU_V4_API_KEY=
